{
  "Name": "BlockSQLiBody",
  "Priority": 10,
  "Action": { "Block": {} },
  "Statement": {
    "SqliMatchStatement": {
      "FieldToMatch": {
        "JsonBody": {
          "MatchPattern": { "All": {} },
          "MatchScope": "VALUE",
          "InvalidFallbackBehavior": "EVALUATE_AS_STRING"
        }
      },
      "TextTransformations": [
        { "Type": "URL_DECODE", "Priority": 0 },
        { "Type": "HTML_ENTITY_DECODE", "Priority": 1 }
      ]
    }
  }
}

**Explanation**: This rule uses `SqliMatchStatement`, which is specifically designed to detect SQL injection patterns. It inspects the values of all fields in the JSON body (the most common place for SQLi in APIs). `TextTransformations` decode URL encoding and HTML entities to catch obfuscated attacks. When matched, the request is immediately blocked, preventing the payload from reaching the backend.
